  "question": {
    "text": "Locus of a centriod of the triangle whose vertices are $(a \\cos t, a \\sin t),(b \\sin t,-b \\cos t)$ and $(1,0)$, where $t$ is a parameter, is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wL68V",
      "text": "\n$(3 x+1)^2+(3 y)^2=a^2-b^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "niDQz",
      "text": "\n$(3 x-1)^2+(3 y)^2=a^2-b^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EsL7o",
      "text": "\n$(3 x-1)^2+(3 y)^2=a^2+b^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "jb4AW",
      "text": "\n$(3 x+1)^2+(3 y)^2=a^2+b^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$x=\\frac{\\cos t+b \\sin t+1}{3} \\Rightarrow a \\cos t+b \\sin t=3 x-1$\n$y=\\frac{a \\sin t-b \\cos t}{3} \\Rightarrow a \\sin t-b \\sin t=3 y$\nSquaring \\& adding, $(3 \\mathrm{x}-1)^2+(3 \\mathrm{y})^2=\\mathrm{a}^2+\\mathrm{b}^2$",
    "image": null
